9 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/348\")\n\n  Line 22455: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0005026 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/800\")\n\n  Line 22668: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/583\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0007021 \"club cell (zebrafish)\")\n\n  Line 22669: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN-10:0412429403\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/583\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0007021 \"club cell\")\n\n  Line 22888: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0008029 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1540>)\n\n  Line 22897: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0008030 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1540>)\n\n  Line 23159: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0009003 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/710\")\n\n  Line 24188: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0009101 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1472\")\n\n  Line 24200: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0009102 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1472\")\n\n  Line 24211: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0009103 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1472\")\n\n  Line 24225: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0009104 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1472\")\n\n  Line 24238: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0009105 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1472\")\n\n  Line 24253: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0009106 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1472\")\n\n  Line 24351: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0009115 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1472\")\n\n  Line 24366: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/417>) obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0010000 \"A hair follicle matrix region cell which synthesizes keratin and undergoes a characteristic change as it moves upward from the hair bulb to become the hair medulla cortex and hair root sheath.\")\n\n  Line 24390: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0010003 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2429>)\n\n  Line 24434: SubClassOf(Annotation(rdfs:seeAlso \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2245\") obo:CL_0010009 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000966))\n\n  Line 24462: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0010012 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1359\")\n\n  Line 24496: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0010017 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/786>)\n\n  Line 25061: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0017501 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/734>)\n\n  Line 25098: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0017505 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2251>)\n\n  Line 26346: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_1000383 \"FMA:263196\")\n\n  Line 28224: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_1001566 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1443>)\n\n  Line 29396: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_2000082 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1562>)\n\n  Line 30419: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_4023073 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2043>)\n\n  Line 33504: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19906678\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21865647\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26964064\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28066889\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047042 \"An enteric glial cell located within the myenteric ganglia of the gastrointestinal tract. This cell has a small somata and has very short, irregularly branched processes that surround neuron cell bodies, giving it a protoplasmic-like appearance. It plays crucial roles in modulating myenteric neuron activity, regulating oxidative stress, and influencing neuroinflammation and neurogenesis.\")\n\n  Line 33507: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4047042 \"type 1 MP\")\n\n  Line 33514: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.3389/fncel.2023.1170309\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28487635\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047043 \"An enteric glial cell that is associated with neuron cell bodies within submucosal ganglia of the gastrointestinal tract. This cell is located in the submucosa, a layer of connective tissue beneath the intestinal mucosa. This cell plays a role in modulating secretomotor neuron activity and contributes to the regulation of digestive fluid secretion and absorption.\")\n\n  Line 33517: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4047043 \"type I SMP\")\n\n  Line 33524: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1002/glia.22876\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35111752\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047044 \"An enteric glial cell that has an elongated, fibrous morphology with long processes that run parallel to nerve fibers connecting enteric myenteric ganglia. This cell is located in the interganglionic fiber tracts of the enteric nervous system.\")\n\n  Line 33534: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25161129\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37153631\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38957473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047045 \"An enteric glial cell located in the lamina propria of the intestinal mucosa. This cell plays important roles in maintaining gut barrier function, regulating intestinal homeostasis, and mediating interactions between the enteric nervous system and the immune system.\")\n\n  Line 33543: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1016/j.celrep.2023.112194\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29927320\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35111752\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047047 \"An enteric glial cell located within the ganglia of the enteric nervous system. This cell is characterized by it’s small somata and short, irregularly branched processes that surround neuronal cell bodies in the myenteric and submucosal ganglia. This cell plays important roles in modulating neuronal activity and neurogenesis in the gastrointestinal tract.\")\n\n  Line 33546: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4047047 \"intraganglionic glia\")\n\n  Line 33555: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34401661\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047048 \"An enteric glial cell characterized by a small central soma that extends long, thin, bipolar projections. This cell is primarily located along small nerve fibers within the muscle layers of the gastrointestinal tract and is known for its unbranching processes that closely follow these nerve fibers in the muscularis.\")\n\n  Line 34690: SubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/757>) ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_7742)) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000031))\n","metadata":{"matches":91,"truncated":false},"title":"3196|term_tracker|github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues|issue/3196","time":{"start":1778977333561,"end":1778977333585}},"id":"prt_e334fe134001sRMyUKfZklZJvm","sessionID":"ses_1ccb0a604ffetWFnLzVrOWuran","messageID":"msg_e334fc72c001JqJ38wS5882B6d"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778977333702,"sessionID":"ses_1ccb0a604ffetWFnLzVrOWuran","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_TkGXQp8Xn6u7yQblK9NpInad","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","offset":31218,"limit":30},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n31218: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030005 \"kidney collecting duct beta-intercalated cell\")\n31219: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4030005 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0002201 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0004203)))\n31220: \n31221: # Class: obo:CL_4030006 (fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell)\n31222: \n31223: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1186/1477-7827-7-129\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.3390/cells8080933\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/learn/dictionary/normal/fallopian+tube\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030006 \"An epithelial cell that is part of the fallopian tube that secretes mucus and oviduct-specific products in response to hormonal stimulation from estrogen and luteinizing hormone. This fallopian tube secretory cell is similar in height to the ciliated cell, but typically exhibits a more narrow, columnar shape. Its nucleus is ovoid and oriented perpendicular to the cell's long axis, with denser chromatin and a smaller nucleolus compared to the ciliated cell.\")\n31224: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4030006 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473>)\n31225: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4030006 \"2022-03-03T10:39:31Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n31226: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4030006 \"oviduct secretory epithelial cell\")\n31227: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030006 \"uterine tube secretory epithelial cell\")\n31228: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ccr.2013.10.013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/learn/dictionary/normal/fallopian+tube\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4030006 \"The other cell types of the fallopian tube epithelium include the ciliated cell and the intercalary cell, or peg cell. The fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell type has been implicated as a source of high-grade serous ovarian carcinoma.\")\n31229: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030006 \"fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell\")\n31230: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030006 obo:CL_1001591)\n31231: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030006 obo:CL_4052019)\n31232: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030006 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0003889))\n31233: \n31234: # Class: obo:CL_4030007 (fallopian tube multiciliated epithelial cell)\n31235: \n31236: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16565155\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/humanproteome/tissue/fallopian+tube\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030007 \"A multi-ciliated epithelial cell that is part of the fallopian tube, mainly found on the apex of the mucosal folds. This cell exhibits a columnar shape with an oval nucleus and is characterized by the presence of cilia on its surface. The coordinated beating of these cilia, together with peristaltic contractions, contributes to the self-propulsion of spermatozoa, the transport of ovum during ovulation and the transport of the fertilized ovum to the intramural fallopian tube.\")\n31237: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4030007 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473>)\n31238: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4030007 \"2022-03-08T12:40:19Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n31239: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4030007 \"oviduct ciliated cell\")\n31240: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030007 \"fallopian tube ciliated cell\")\n31241: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030007 \"fallopian tube multiciliated cell\")\n31242: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030007 \"uterine tube ciliated epithelial cell\")\n31243: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030007 \"fallopian tube multiciliated epithelial cell\")\n31244: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030007 obo:CL_0005012)\n31245: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030007 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0003889))\n31246: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030007 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0007589))\n31247: \n\n(Showing lines 31218-31247 of 34691. Use offset=31248 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030005 \"kidney collecting duct beta-intercalated cell\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4030005 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0002201 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0004203)))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_4030006 (fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1186/1477-7827-7-129\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.3390/cells8080933\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/learn/dictionary/normal/fallopian+tube\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030006 \"An epithelial cell that is part of the fallopian tube that secretes mucus and oviduct-specific products in response to hormonal stimulation from estrogen and luteinizing hormone. This fallopian tube secretory cell is similar in height to the ciliated cell, but typically exhibits a more narrow, columnar shape. Its nucleus is ovoid and oriented perpendicular to the cell's long axis, with denser chromatin and a smaller nucleolus compared to the ciliated cell.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4030006 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4030006 \"2022-03-03T10:39:31Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4030006 \"oviduct secretory epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030006 \"uterine tube secretory epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ccr.2013.10.013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/learn/dictionary/normal/fallopian+tube\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4030006 \"The other cell types of the fallopian tube epithelium include the ciliated cell and the intercalary cell, or peg cell. The fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell type has been implicated as a source of high-grade serous ovarian carcinoma.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030006 \"fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4030006 obo:CL_1001591)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4030006 obo:CL_4052019)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4030006 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0003889))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_4030007 (fallopian tube multiciliated epithelial cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16565155\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/humanproteome/tissue/fallopian+tube\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030007 \"A multi-ciliated epithelial cell that is part of the fallopian tube, mainly found on the apex of the mucosal folds. This cell exhibits a columnar shape with an oval nucleus and is characterized by the presence of cilia on its surface. The coordinated beating of these cilia, together with peristaltic contractions, contributes to the self-propulsion of spermatozoa, the transport of ovum during ovulation and the transport of the fertilized ovum to the intramural fallopian tube.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4030007 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473>)","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"title":"src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","time":{"start":1778977333536,"end":1778977333700}},"id":"prt_e334fe11a001L67fAY5h8k094R","sessionID":"ses_1ccb0a604ffetWFnLzVrOWuran","messageID":"msg_e334fc72c001JqJ38wS5882B6d"}}
