{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778977483745,"sessionID":"ses_1ccb0a604ffetWFnLzVrOWuran","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_MbmuDqFH89Ej4mQFN1DGcEoY","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Added a new CL term for `dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell` with the reviewed label, definition, synonyms, issue link, contributor ORCID, and a logical definition placing it as a human fallopian tube epithelial progenitor that develops into fallopian tube secretory and multiciliated epithelial cells.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Implemented issue #3196 by adding a new NTR term to `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`:\n+\n+- `CL_9900001` `dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell`\n+\n+What I changed:\n+\n+- Added the agreed primary label from the issue discussion.\n+- Added a textual definition based on the reviewed wording in the issue comments, with `PMID:40475517` as the supporting reference.\n+- Added the requested contributor ORCID: `0000-0002-1482-1032`.\n+- Added the required timestamp for a new CL term.\n+- Added `dc:creator \"GitHub Copilot\"` for the new term only.\n+- Linked the term back to issue `#3196` using `IAO:0000233` and the issue URL pattern already used in the ontology.\n+- Added synonyms reflecting both the historical issue submission and prior literature:\n+  - related: `non-ciliated secretory epithelial cell 2-1 (NCSE2-1 cells)` [`PMID:35320732`]\n+  - related: `non-ciliated secretory epithelial cell 2-2 (NCSE2-2 cells)` [`PMID:35320732`]\n+  - related acronym: `UCFP` [`PMID:40475517`]\n+  - exact: `unclassified fallopian tube progenitor` [`PMID:40475517`]\n+- Added a genus-differentia logical definition using existing CL/UBERON terms:\n+  - genus: `progenitor cell` (`CL_0011026`)\n+  - `part of` some `fallopian tube epithelium` (`UBERON_0007589`)\n+  - `in taxon` some `Homo sapiens` (`NCBITaxon_9606`)\n+  - `develops into` some `fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell` (`CL_4030006`)\n+  - `develops into` some `fallopian tube multiciliated epithelial cell` (`CL_4030007`)\n+\n+Rationale:\n+\n+- The issue discussion converged on `dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell` as the preferred CL label.\n+- The requested parent candidates (`CL_4052018` / `CL_4052019`) were less precise than the reviewed logical definition. Modeling this term as a `progenitor cell` located in fallopian tube epithelium and developing into the two established epithelial fates better matches the reviewed issue text and existing CL logical-definition practices.\n+- I used `fallopian tube epithelium` rather than the broader `fallopian tube` anatomical context because the reviewed logical definition in the issue explicitly specified epithelium, and the source paper describes the population within primary human fallopian tube epithelium.\n+\n+Checks completed:\n+\n+- Read `__issue_context__.json` for the issue title, body, and comments.\n+- Checked existing fallopian tube epithelial and progenitor-related terms in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` to avoid duplicating an existing class and to reuse existing IDs.\n+- Reviewed the cited literature context from `PMID:40475517` and `PMID:35320732`.\n+- Validated syntax locally with:\n+  - `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit.ofn`\n+\n+Commit created locally:\n+\n+- `f6ee20e` `Add dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell`\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Added a new CL term for `dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell` with the reviewed label, definition, synonyms, issue link, contributor ORCID, and a logical definition placing it as a human fallopian tube epithelial progenitor that develops into fallopian tube secretory and multiciliated epithelial cells.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@\n+Implemented issue #3196 by adding a new NTR term to `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`:\n+\n+- `CL_9900001` `dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell`\n+\n+What I changed:\n+\n+- Added the agreed primary label from the issue discussion.\n+- Added a textual definition based on the reviewed wording in the issue comments, with `PMID:40475517` as the supporting reference.\n+- Added the requested contributor ORCID: `0000-0002-1482-1032`.\n+- Added the required timestamp for a new CL term.\n+- Added `dc:creator \"GitHub Copilot\"` for the new term only.\n+- Linked the term back to issue `#3196` using `IAO:0000233` and the issue URL pattern already used in the ontology.\n+- Added synonyms reflecting both the historical issue submission and prior literature:\n+  - related: `non-ciliated secretory epithelial cell 2-1 (NCSE2-1 cells)` [`PMID:35320732`]\n+  - related: `non-ciliated secretory epithelial cell 2-2 (NCSE2-2 cells)` [`PMID:35320732`]\n+  - related acronym: `UCFP` [`PMID:40475517`]\n+  - exact: `unclassified fallopian tube progenitor` [`PMID:40475517`]\n+- Added a genus-differentia logical definition using existing CL/UBERON terms:\n+  - genus: `progenitor cell` (`CL_0011026`)\n+  - `part of` some `fallopian tube epithelium` (`UBERON_0007589`)\n+  - `in taxon` some `Homo sapiens` (`NCBITaxon_9606`)\n+  - `develops into` some `fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell` (`CL_4030006`)\n+  - `develops into`